  "workflow_name": "First-principles point defect characterization",
  "definition": "This workflow family uses density functional theory (DFT) with supercell models to compute electronic structure and thermodynamic properties of point defects in crystalline solids. The common procedure includes constructing a supercell, introducing a defect (vacancy, substitution, interstitial, or complex), relaxing atomic positions, calculating total energies for various charge states, and deriving defect formation energies, transition levels, and electronic density of states. The results enable analysis of defect stability, doping behavior, and impact on material properties.",
